Command:        Vote
Purpose:        Move to the Vote area
Available at:   Main>

The Vote area is a place where users may express their opinions on any number of various polls, questionaires, or surveys.  After voting, you always have the option of changing your vote.

If so configured, you may be able to add your own vote topics to the Vote area.  Follow the prompts as they are given to you.  Once you have added a topic, you may Kill or Edit it as you see necessary.

Each system subboard may have an optional set of Vote topics linked to specific post items.  Users with sufficient access may create special vote topics linked to posts.  At the respond prompt, typing "vote" allows users to then vote on the linked topic.  The subboard vote topics are kept separate from the main ones and can ONLY be seen from the subboards.
